; coverage test for set.kurt's "function-space"/"function-space-def": a mapping is modelled as
; an opaque, applicable set object (kurt's ordinary space-application, `$f $a`), and `A → B` is
; the set of all such objects that map every element of A into B.
load set
const A, B, f

use ∀ $a  ($a ∈ A implies (f $a) ∈ B)
f ∈ (A → B)
f : A → B
;;; Proof checked.
